# `h := e` is charged (P71, wiki/charged.md): evaluated at each use, so it follows the variables it reads, through words

'g = 1; h := g * 10; g = 2; h'	20
'g = 1; h := g * 10; k := h + 1; g = 2; k'	21
'g = 1; f(n) := n * g; h := f(3); g = 5; h'	15
'c := 5 * 2; c'	10
'try { eval("x := 1; x = 2; x") } catch e { is_error(e) }'	1	P71: assigning a := name afterwards is an error (card p71-says)
'use sound; tuning = 442; A4'	442
